.TH "ODIR-DOT-SQLSCHEMA" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-dot\-sqlschema \- \&.sqlschema: Show catalog schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.sqlschema [table=<table>] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows every column of the tables in the public schema of the catalog database with its data type, ordered by table and column position; table= restricts the output to one table. An unknown table yields an empty list, a name that is not a plain identifier is rejected. The command only reads and helps writing queries for .sql.
.PP
Onesimus extension: Bareos does not know the command and answers ".sqlschema: is an invalid command.". Besides .sqlschema in its Command ACL the console needs .sql or sqlquery, as for any raw catalog access.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "\&.sqlschema"
.TP
.B "table=<table>"
Table name (text)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "\&.sqlschema table=pool"
columns and data types of the pool table
.TP
.B "\&.sqlschema"
the columns of every catalog table
.SH ORIGIN
Onesimus extension. The Bareos Director does not know this command and answers "is an invalid command".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir\-commands (7),
.BR oconsole (1)
